.TH CHAIN\-TABLE 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
chain\-table \- print the chain registry (crates/core chains.rs) as data, one JSON object per
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
chain\-table [\-\-array | NAME]: the chain registry as JSON (public data, no keys)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
chain: name, ticker, SLIP\-44 coin type, curve, address encoding and version bytes / hrp,
signer kind, whether tx\-build signs it, verified flag and parameter source. Public data only.
`chain\-table` = JSON lines; `chain\-table \-\-array` = one JSON array; `chain\-table NAME` = one row.
.SH WARNING
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
.br
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
.br
It opens hostile wallet files and extracts secrets: run it only sealed and offline (./blocktools run).
.br
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, recipes/README.md
